# File: tests/features/add_public_greeting_has_double_quote_helper.feature
# Generated from: specs/171-add-public-greeting-has-double-quote-helper/requirements.md
Feature: Detect a literal double quote in a completed greeting

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Detect literal double quote in a completed greeting
    Given the public greeting package and valid name Ada"
    When greeting_has_double_quote is called with Ada"
    Then greet returns Hello, Ada" and the helper returns True

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Reject absent and fullwidth double quotes
    Given valid names Ada and Ada＂
    When greeting_has_double_quote is called with each valid name
    Then each completed greeting lacks literal double quote and each helper result is False

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Preserve greet validation for invalid names
    Given invalid names empty, whitespace-only, None, and 42
    When greeting_has_double_quote is called with each invalid name
    Then each call raises ValueError with message name must not be blank

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Import and run documented helper examples
    Given the installed public package and README Library examples Ada" and Ada
    When greeting_has_double_quote is imported from nmg_sdlc_smoke and called with those names
    Then the imported helper returns True and False respectively
